    "resilience": 3,
    "pilot": 2
  },
  "strategy": "Ghoulcaller Gisa turns one creature into many: sacrifice a Zombie, get that many 2/2 Zombies back. The deck is a wide black Zombie board built around that trade. Lords like Death Baron, Lord of the Undead and Undead Warchief make every token a threat, Cryptbreaker, Midnight Reaper and Graveborn Muse turn the bodies into cards, and Gravecrawler, Cemetery Recruitment and Oversold Cemetery bring the good ones back. Kalitas steals the opponents' dead as Zombies of its own, and Gray Merchant of Asphodel drains the table for the devotion the board has built. It plays slowly and grinds: the plan is to outlast a wrath with a graveyard full of returns, then swing wide with an anthem out.",
  "signature": [
    {
      "card_id": "ghoulcaller_gisa",
      "why": "Sacrifice a Zombie, make that many Zombies: the engine is the commander."
    },
    {
      "card_id": "gray_merchant_of_asphodel",
      "why": "A board of black permanents is devotion, and every point drains each opponent."
    },
    {
      "card_id": "kalitas_traitor_of_ghet",
      "why": "Opponents' creatures die as Zombies on your side of the table."
    },
    {
      "card_id": "death_baron",
      "why": "Every Zombie gets bigger and gains deathtouch, so nothing blocks the horde cleanly."
    }
  ],
